My Student Portfolio

A responsive student portfolio website built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

About the Project:

This is my first frontend web development project, created to learn and practice the fundamentals of building websites.

The portfolio includes sections for my introduction, skills, projects, goals, and contact information.

Features:

- Responsive layout for desktop and mobile screens
- Navigation between different sections
- Interactive buttons using JavaScript
- Show/hide functionality for skills and goals
- Contact form with basic validation
- GitHub project link

Technologies Used:

- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- Git
- GitHub

What I Learned:

Through this project, I learned the fundamentals of frontend web development, including:

- Structuring webpages using HTML
- Styling webpages using CSS
- Creating responsive layouts using media queries
- Adding interactivity using JavaScript
- Handling basic form validation
- Using Git and GitHub to manage and publish a project

Learning Outcome:

This project helped me understand how HTML, CSS, and JavaScript work together to create a responsive and interactive website. It also gave me my first practical experience with Git and GitHub.
